# Shell scripts must keep LF line endings in the working copy.
#
# CI runs .github/scripts/*.sh under bash on BOTH ubuntu-latest and
# windows-latest. Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which would
# check these out with CRLF; bash then fails on every line with
# `$'\r': command not found`. Scoped to *.sh deliberately — a repo-wide
# `* text=auto` would renormalise every file in the tree and collide with every
# in-flight branch.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Vendored third-party browser assets (GH-200). Byte-exact on every platform:
# tests/test_no_external_subresources.py verifies each file against a recorded
# sha256, and CRLF conversion would change those bytes. lucide-1.28.0.min.js
# carries 12 LF bytes, so without this a Windows checkout would produce a
# different hash than a Linux one and the guard would fail on one leg only.
admz/api/static/vendor/** -text
